{
  "content": {
    "items": [
      {
        "description": "Before working any pebble, table or checklist, list every unit (field, ref, requirement, step) with a count. Processing before enumeration is a violation — it is where skipping hides.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "0a8a9713-9fdc-406f-b113-71491d72892a",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Enumerate before processing"
      },
      {
        "description": "done · n/a (reason) · blocked (reason). Silence is not a disposition; a unit you didn't mention is a unit you skipped.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "b09b0dba-4687-4e5b-97b7-4f8eea7765bc",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Every unit gets an explicit disposition"
      },
      {
        "description": "End with \"covered N of M enumerated units\". If N < M, name the gap and continue or escalate — never report success over a gap.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "ca88471f-e933-40f1-a318-494a883893c6",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Reconcile counts before finishing"
      },
      {
        "description": "Read the full pebble plus its outbound refs before forming conclusions, and cite which refs you actually opened. No judgment from the first half.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "3696dfe9-4833-4480-8dfb-cfd73fd8070a",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Read artifacts whole, refs included"
      },
      {
        "description": "If size forces batching, declare the chunk plan up front and reconcile per chunk. Chunking is fine; invisible truncation is not.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "6912da27-e97a-4df4-ac01-1d3be24ac441",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Chunk honestly"
      },
      {
        "description": "\"etc.\", \"and others\", or an elided list in output is a violation — expand it or count it explicitly.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "04496389-c585-4a27-8d0b-8914a9846594",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "No ellipsis in results"
      }
    ],
    "kind": "checklist"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.686Z",
  "description": "Partial attention is the root defect: skipped fields, skipped refs, half-read pebbles. Enumeration-first and count reconciliation make every skip visible and self-correcting.",
  "id": "e393db14-c215-4774-b752-6d09c864d3e3",
  "name": "Total attention — no skipping",
  "refs": [
    {
      "id": "199c9c27-c3cb-4660-8215-b4375634aa3e",
      "label": "Pebbles platform overview",
      "path": ".pebbles/knowledge/system/platform-overview.pebble",
      "pebbleId": "0666d6bf-0891-49a1-93f8-b4cac16ecd57",
      "section": "knowledge",
      "targetKind": "pebble"
    }
  ],
